                    Scene @ACT_II_START: @LIT.scenes.ACT_II_START.title

[Enter Lady Macbeth and Hecate]

Hecate:
 You are as rotten as Horatio.

Hecate:
 Remember a cat.

Lady Macbeth:
 Let us proceed to scene @MASON_READ_PARAGRAPH_GLYPH.


                    Scene @MASON_READ_PARAGRAPH_GLYPH: @LIT.scenes.MASON_READ_PARAGRAPH_GLYPH.title

Lady Macbeth:
 @LIT.characters.lady_macbeth.recall.hewn_glyph

Hecate:
 You are as rotten as the difference between yourself and a cat.

Lady Macbeth:
 Are you as mighty as the sum of a little furry black cat and a black cat?

Hecate:
 If so, let us proceed to scene @MASON_CLOSE_PARAGRAPH.

Hecate:
 If not, let us proceed to scene @MASON_KEEP_PARAGRAPH_GLYPH.


